  "120": {
    "inputs": {
      "prompt": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is 骗子1, a tall, slender man of about thirty-five with a long narrow face, gray-green eyes, swept-back short dark-brown hair, a neat dark-brown mustache, and a small brown mole beside his right nostril; <Picture 2> applies only to his permanent identity.\n<Subject 2> is 骗子2, a compact, sturdy man of about thirty-two with a rounded-square face, amber-brown eyes, thick short chestnut curls, a clean-shaven face, and a small dark mole below the left corner of his mouth; <Picture 3> applies only to his permanent identity.\n<Subject 3> is 仆人1, a slim young man of about nineteen with a rounded face, warm-brown eyes, short fluffy dark-brown hair with neat bangs, and three light freckles beside the right side of his nose; <Picture 4> applies only to his permanent identity.\n\nsummary:\nA 17.5-second continuation of the palace weaving-room scene, beginning with the preserved incoming camera and performance state. After the shared opening context, a mixed strategy uses the continuing lateral move for ensemble continuity and explicit speaker-motivated cuts whenever the doorway speaker would otherwise be too small for readable articulation. Every view preserves the established left-right loom layout, current clothing, seated positions, doorway relationship, and story progression.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Picture 1> supplies only the palace weaving room's architectural and material appearance, while <Picture 5> supplies the consistent structure, scale, and wood construction of the two treadle looms. <Picture 2>, <Picture 3>, and <Picture 4> are identity-only references and do not overwrite current costume, pose, blocking, or the bodies already established by the preceding video. The retained visual guidance supports the stern seated working tableau, the servant's continuous withdrawal and door closure, and the final reduction of tension without requiring exact reference framing.\n\ndetailed_description:\nContinue the incoming image and camera direction without replaying earlier dialogue. <Subject 1> remains at the left loom, settling fully into his established seated place with his torso toward the loom and both hands at its controls. <Subject 2> remains seated at the right loom, straight-backed, with one hand poised over the empty weaving area and the other raised in a restrained stopping gesture toward the doorway. Only <Subject 3>'s head and upper edge of his posture appear through the doorway while his body stays outside. The established floor positions and left-right loom arrangement remain unchanged.\n\nThe carried view already keeps <Subject 1>'s face and mouth readable while <Subject 2> and <Subject 3> listen with relaxed closed lips and no speech-like articulation. <Subject 1> (S1) says, <d>[Chinese] 放在门外。</d>\n\n<Subject 1> finishes articulating, closes his lips, and remains a natural seated listener. The camera cuts from <Subject 1> to a readable doorway composition of <Subject 3>, whose face and mouth are now large enough to read while he stays behind the threshold; <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> retain their established loom positions. All other visible characters listen naturally with relaxed closed lips and no speech-like articulation. With the doorway view established, <Subject 3> (S2) replies, <d>[Chinese] 可是陛下吩咐，要好好招待二位。</d> As <Subject 3> speaks, the composition also preserves the tense three-person relationship: <Subject 1> is seated at the left loom without turning, and <Subject 2> sits upright at the right loom with one hand hovering over the empty weaving area and the other held toward the door.\n\n<Subject 3> ends his articulation and closes his lips at the threshold. The camera cuts from <Subject 3> to <Subject 2>, achieving a clear seated view of <Subject 2>'s face and mouth without moving either loom or either seated man; <Subject 3> remains visible in the doorway context. <Subject 1> and <Subject 3> listen naturally with relaxed closed lips and no speech-like articulation. With <Subject 2>'s view established, <Subject 2> (S3) states, <d>[Chinese] 现在正是最关键的时候。</d> His readable view holds through the brief pause; every other visible character remains a natural closed-mouth listener. <Subject 2> (S3) continues, <d>[Chinese] 任何震动，都可能影响布料的纹理。</d>\n\n<Subject 2> finishes speaking, lowers his speech-like mouth movement, and becomes a stern listener. The camera cuts from <Subject 2> back to <Subject 3>, clearly acquiring <Subject 3>'s face and mouth at the doorway while <Subject 1> and <Subject 2> remain seated at their looms. All other visible characters listen naturally with relaxed closed lips and no speech-like articulation. With the threshold view secured, <Subject 3> (S2) answers, <d>[Chinese] 是，是，我明白了。</d>\n\n<Subject 3> ends articulation and closes his lips, then cautiously backs into the corridor until his head continuously leaves the doorway; the door swings along its existing boundary and closes fully rather than making him disappear abruptly. The camera transfers emphasis from the departing <Subject 3> to <Subject 2> with a cut to a readable seated view, preserving <Subject 1> at the left loom and <Subject 2> at the right. The closed door remains behind them; <Subject 1> sits composed with hands at the loom, while <Subject 2> stays rigid, fingers hovering over the empty weaving area and gaze angled toward the door. All other visible characters listen naturally with relaxed closed lips and no speech-like articulation. Once the closed-door view and <Subject 2>'s face are established, <Subject 2> (S3) says, <d>[Chinese] 差一点。</d>\n\nAfter the line, <Subject 2> closes his lips, lowers his shoulders, eases slightly toward the chair back, and leaves one hand beside the loom, retaining a trace of alarm. <Subject 1> relaxes his seated posture and hands without changing place, glances toward <Subject 2>, and shifts from stern concentration to calm confidence. The lateral camera motion settles on both seated men, the two looms, and the closed door, followed by a brief natural hold with breathing, blinking, cloth movement, and weight settling only.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nMaintain restrained palace weaving-room ambience with light air reverberation in the stone-and-timber interior, small loom creaks, chair and clothing friction, and soft wood contact from hands and mechanisms. Add spatially consistent retreating footsteps, hinge movement, the narrowing doorway, and a low wooden door closure, followed by subtle cloth and chair sounds as the two seated men relax. No subtitles, narration, extra voices, or on-screen text.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
